  ],
  "method": "Two runs of Scripts/livekit/live_1092_rewind_and_forward_step_one_bar.py at 229c08f1f4629a52bb9704d6c755460beb967c65, with no LOGIC_MCP_DEBUG_ONLY_CHANNEL. The first drove a debug build of that head (sha256 e190e924ecaf4f41949005ee2930c1ebd51bf35ab5fd395aaac2952b2762caf2) in ten languages, three trials each; the second drove a debug build of the merge-base 45910dc28751e34054e39d1bcf909d7156d547c3 (sha256 4a05330ab93028328d1bf899e0606f26d233a6819efaf3fc19007ff539082032) in ko and en, two trials each, as the control. For each language Logic was quit, its AppleLanguages set, and the lpm-locale-campaign fixture reopened. Each trial stopped the transport, moved the playhead to bar 9 through transport.goto_position and read it back, made the call, and read the bar 0.5, 1.5 and 3.0 s after the reply. The bar was read by the harness process from Logic's control bar (the playhead group's bar slider), not from the server. The channels that ran were read from the call's operation trace (channel.started events), not from the reply. Each binary was built at a clean checkout of its commit with that commit embedded in the Mach-O section __TEXT,__lpm_commit; the harness read the section from the measured file and refused to drive a binary whose commit was not the head it was given (observations[0].artifacts). A row passes when the bar read 9 before, the reply succeeded, CGEvent was the only channel that ran, and all three readings were the bar one away in the call's direction. Each row's check was run against its own observation and against the same row with the shuttle readings the MCU rung gave in ko earlier that day, which it must reject.",
